 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\nThe billing schema extension is an entity in SAP IS-U contract billing that is integrated in the billing schema according to the data\nmodel. The billing schema extension contains the conditional billing program and the rate relationship group with the rate\nrelationships.\n\nYou establish which rates are billed and the order in which they are to be processed in the billing schema. You define the\nrelationship between these rates in the billing schema extension: Which rates are used as basic rates for the entire billing period\nand which rates are only used as conditional rates for active TOU exceptions to supplement or substitute the basic rates. Basic\nrates and conditional rates must be used in the same schema and be defined with the same relationship in rate determination.\n\nThe conditional billing program defined in the billing schema extension is used to activate conditional rates. Assigning conditional\nbilling programs to TOU exception programs executes the corresponding rates in the billing schema extension for an active TOU\nexception.\n\nMore Information\n\nRate Relationships\n\nConditional Billing Program\n\nActivities\n\nCreate Billing Schema Extension\n\nConditional Billing Program\n\nThe conditional billing program is used to activate conditional rates for an active TOU exception.\n\nYou define the conditional billing program in the billing schema extension and assign it to TOU exception programs. The conditional\nbilling program refers to a billing schema. You also assign conditional rates to the conditional billing program. These assignments\nmean the system executes the corresponding conditional rates for the billing schema extension for an active TOU exception.\n\nThe conditional billing program means rates can be controlled with a greater degree of flexibility during an exception period. You\ncan assign the conditional billing program to several rate relationship groups and several TOU exception programs. This gives you\nseveral options for representing specific contract conditions and different types of rates including those for interval customers.\n\nRate Relationships\n\nUse\n\nIn conditional billing, the relationship between rates plays a very important role. Rates are used as basic rates for the entire billing\n\nperiod. They are only used as conditional rates for active time-of-use exceptions in order to supplement or substitute the basic\nrates. Rate relationships between basic rates and conditional rates are defined in the billing schema extension.\n\nRate Relationship Groups\n\nThe rate relationship group specifies a rate fact group to combine a basic rate with all conditional rates that are assigned to this\n",
